                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "805301b8-c40a-370e-b921-972d2fc22dd4",
                        "entry_id": "74e438f6-ce47-36bb-9e07-46dfa2e1a9f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. лицо, принадлежавшее к исконным римским родам, составлявшим правящий класс и державшим в своих руках общественные земли"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "в Древнем Риме"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee8e0892-144e-447f-82e6-d7b1d9d20d30",
                                "sense_id": "805301b8-c40a-370e-b921-972d2fc22dd4",
                                "text": "С превращением Рима в мировое государство к патрициям присоединяется быстро разбогатевшее на ростовщичестве, откупах сословие всадников."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fffa4e2e-ea88-4063-86b0-141106b15820",
                                "sense_id": "805301b8-c40a-370e-b921-972d2fc22dd4",
                                "text": "А древнеримский врач Скрибоний, говорят, небезуспешно излечивал подагру стареющих римских патрициев с помощью «освежающего» удара электрического угря."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "92e243f3-6824-36c6-b1bb-6a1fb2edc2f1",
                        "entry_id": "74e438f6-ce47-36bb-9e07-46dfa2e1a9f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. лицо, принадлежавшее к зажиточным бюргерским родам, игравшим первенствующую роль в самоуправлении"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "в городах Германии в эпоху Средневековья"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ef992ec-c088-4862-8dff-f634f459357e",
                                "sense_id": "92e243f3-6824-36c6-b1bb-6a1fb2edc2f1",
                                "text": "Несмотря на то, что по происхождению своему он принадлежал к местным патрициям и аристократам, отец Артура был проникнут идеями справедливости и свободы, что стяжало ему расположение и любовь его сограждан."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc606a16-2da0-4428-9683-805f00844219",
                        "source_entry_id": "74e438f6-ce47-36bb-9e07-46dfa2e1a9f8",
                        "source_sense_description": "лицо, принадлежавшее к исконным римским родам, составлявшим правящий класс",
                        "target_lang_word": "patrician",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "patrician",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36deb2e9-0db2-374e-862e-b3a54284b907",
                                        "entry_id": "e8a0fa85-5c9e-3d92-a170-c47849ccfc21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of any of the families constituting the populus Romanus, or body of Roman citizens, before the development of the plebeian order; later, one who, by right of birth or by special privilege conferred, belonged to the senior class of Romans, who, with certain property, had by right a seat in the Roman Senate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Rome"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "246e593a-1f80-49fc-b742-43bd5bf3d004",
                                                "sense_id": "36deb2e9-0db2-374e-862e-b3a54284b907",
                                                "text": "Noble Patricians, Patrons of my right, / Defend the iuſtice of my Cauſe with Armes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cfd8379-0e29-3c79-84b0-39f8d8c5e39a",
                                        "entry_id": "e8a0fa85-5c9e-3d92-a170-c47849ccfc21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person of high birth; a nobleman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5057f7d5-c605-368e-a702-7b9cf3a88eb1",
                                        "entry_id": "e8a0fa85-5c9e-3d92-a170-c47849ccfc21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One familiar with the works of the Christian Fathers; one versed in patristic lore or life."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patrician",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ca43aca-a7a2-3eec-bb61-9ee28dbcaff0",
                                        "entry_id": "ce170f4e-e044-37bb-b0a4-b2bb317c50a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the Roman patres (“fathers”) or senators, or patricians."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a909348-6fba-4b7b-804b-e8c7305643ee",
                                                "sense_id": "6ca43aca-a7a2-3eec-bb61-9ee28dbcaff0",
                                                "text": "[…] I ſee\nTh’ Inſulting Tyrant prancing o’er the Field\nStrow’d with Rome’s Citizens, and drench’d in Slaughter,\nHis Horſe’s Hoofs wet with Patrician Blood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64bacf9f-0ff1-4834-90d9-0d776af08feb",
                                                "sense_id": "6ca43aca-a7a2-3eec-bb61-9ee28dbcaff0",
                                                "text": "The cognomen was first used in patrician families, who were distinguished from the plebeians by their three names."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6a6fef0-3c40-364e-8729-b7535f7cab67",
                                        "entry_id": "ce170f4e-e044-37bb-b0a4-b2bb317c50a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to a person of high birth; noble; not plebeian; aristocratic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff34af2a-1e0e-4cc8-b1a4-64f9e56ce835",
                                                "sense_id": "c6a6fef0-3c40-364e-8729-b7535f7cab67",
                                                "text": "born in the patrician file of society"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e02ee923-2033-312a-aae5-28ce03161116",
                                        "entry_id": "ce170f4e-e044-37bb-b0a4-b2bb317c50a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characteristic of or appropriate to a person of high birth; classy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c249cfba-bd1b-49b4-b6b1-27e721abe7f7",
                                                "sense_id": "e02ee923-2033-312a-aae5-28ce03161116",
                                                "text": "Hanks' taste in projects and directors is undoubtedly patrician and with a few exceptions like 1993's Philadelphia, the first mainstream film about the Aids crisis, rarely provocative"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4807efa6-5be5-31c5-9792-11f7febece3f",
                                        "entry_id": "ce170f4e-e044-37bb-b0a4-b2bb317c50a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Politically active to help people in lower classes, especially in a patronizing or condescending way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b199f786-7274-454e-9bcd-ac3d4f217afe",
                                                "sense_id": "4807efa6-5be5-31c5-9792-11f7febece3f",
                                                "text": "It will speed the shrivelling of the patrician “one nation” Tories, who tried to curb the extremes of Thatcherism and ended by providing its veils."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c5ac34c-1c26-4870-8aac-05277c414177",
                                                "sense_id": "4807efa6-5be5-31c5-9792-11f7febece3f",
                                                "text": "Saint-Simon was certainly a radical, and hostile to inherited privilege, but his bourgeois 'socialism' was of a patrician kind. Science, being a firm and certain kind of knowledge, a 'religion of Newton' or 'cult of Reason' essentially plays the key role in his grand scheme for social engineering."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "141befb6-cf09-4545-91ae-d4c9c968266a",
                                                "sense_id": "4807efa6-5be5-31c5-9792-11f7febece3f",
                                                "text": "Where Ruskin's patrician socialism sought to create better conditions and 'higher' aspirations for the 'Workmen and Labourers of Great Britain', Sickert painted his working- and lower-middle-class subjects as if history, in the advance of mass culture and popular democracy, were on their side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
